        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಉಯಿಲು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಯಿಲು — uyilu — \"a will (testament)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜ ಸಾಯುವ ಮುಂಚೆ ಉಯಿಲು ಬರೆದಿದ್ದರು. ajja sāyuva muñce uyilu barediddaru. Grandfather had written a will before he died."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A will is \"written\": ಉಯಿಲು (uyilu) ಬರೆ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಉಯಿಲು (uyilu) is usually traced to English will, the legal paper, which reached the South Indian languages under British courts."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
