          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಾರಸುದಾರ — vārasudāra — \"an heir\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜನ ಮನೆಗೆ ಅವರ ಮೊಮ್ಮಗನೇ ವಾರಸುದಾರ. ajjana manege avara mommaganē vārasudāra. The grandson is the heir to Grandfather's house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ವಾರಸುದಾರರು, vārasudāraru."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "-ದಾರ means \"holder\", as in ಜಮೀನುದಾರ, a landholder."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ವಾರಸುದಾರ (vārasudāra) is a loan from Arabic wāris, \"an heir\", with the Persian ending -dār, \"holder\"; the word came through Hindustani."
            }
          ]
        },
